  "worked_solution": "The difference $P-S$ consists of all the elements that are in $P$ but not $S.$ To represent $P-S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $P$ but not $S.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/3e25daddd75613f6e85f9f46d68f463876edd50f7df11961de8b53e108d5fd88.png)\n\nOnly the element $1$ is in $P$  but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nP-S={1}.\n$$",
